  <prompt>
    UAT round 4 (`notes/UAT-ROUND4-FEEDBACK.md` section B) on the `CommunicationAttachments` PCF
    (`src/client/pcf/CommunicationAttachments/`). Four items:

    B12-1 — reduce the padding ABOVE the section title (title closer to the top of the section boundary).
    B12-2 — increase the padding BELOW the title (more space before the first attachment line). Mirror the same
      asymmetric title-padding convention task 121 applies to Connections + records in UI-DESIGN-STANDARDS.md (read
      that doc; if 121 hasn't updated it yet in your run, apply the same small-top/larger-bottom padding).
    B12-3 — BUG (W11 A11-2 follow-up): the per-row upload icon is NOT rendering distinct green/red — the screenshot
      shows every row the same dark cloud. Root-cause it: the W11 `enrichUploadStatus` reads `sprk_document`
      (`sprk_graphitemid` / `sprk_hasfile`) via an extra `context.webAPI` call. Verify (a) that read actually returns
      those fields (correct logical names, correct filter, not silently failing → all `undefined` → all one state),
      and (b) the icon color is driven by the boolean via Fluent color tokens (`colorPaletteGreenForeground1` /
      `colorPaletteRedForeground1`). Fix so uploaded rows are GREEN and not-uploaded rows are RED, visibly distinct.
      Add a test proving the green/red mapping off the boolean.
    B12-4 — the `.eml` attachment currently shows an external "open in SharePoint" icon and opens externally (the
      `isEmailMessageAttachment` special-case routes it to download instead of the modal). Owner wants it to open the
      SAME in-modal `RichFilePreviewDialog` preview as other attachments. FIRST verify whether
      `GET /api/documents/{id}/preview-url` returns a renderable URL for a `.eml` document (SPE/Graph may preview
      `message/rfc822`). IF it renders, remove the `.eml`/`.msg` download special-case so those rows open the modal
      preview (and appear in the prev/next nav set). IF it genuinely cannot render, STOP and report (do not silently
      leave the external-open behavior — surface the finding).
  </prompt>

  <goal>
    Title sits close to the section top with breathing room below; every attachment row shows a clearly green
    (uploaded) or red (not-uploaded) SPE icon; and `.eml` attachments open the same in-modal preview as other files
    (or the reason they cannot is reported).
  </goal>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Title top padding reduced + bottom padding increased (Fluent tokens), matching the UI-DESIGN-STANDARDS asymmetric convention.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Per-row upload icon renders GREEN when the document has an uploaded SPE file and RED when not — distinct colors via Fluent tokens; the underlying upload-status read is verified to return the field (not all-undefined). A test asserts the green/red mapping off the uploaded boolean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`.eml` rows open the in-modal `RichFilePreviewDialog` (same as other attachments) and participate in prev/next nav — OR, if the preview URL cannot render `.eml`, the task report states that finding with evidence and leaves a documented fallback.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` clean; jest green (upload-status green/red + .eml routing); version bump all 5 locations (1.2.0 → 1.3.0); ZIP repacked + validated (type-66, apostrophe-free).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">§11: still reuses RichFilePreviewDialog (no new modal), upload status from existing webAPI data (no new BFF surface).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <constraints>
    <constraint>ADR-021 Fluent v9 tokens (green/red via `colorPaletteGreenForeground1`/`colorPaletteRedForeground1`); ADR-022; ADR-028 auth.</constraint>
    <constraint>Prefer staying within `src/client/pcf/CommunicationAttachments/**`. Do NOT modify `@spaarke/ui-components` (the W11 `showTitle` double-header fix is already in the shared lib — `.eml` should preview through the existing `RichFilePreviewDialog` unchanged). If a shared-lib change seems needed, STOP and report (avoids racing the parallel W12 shared-lib task).</constraint>
    <constraint>Manifest description-keys generic + apostrophe-free; type-66 solution; follow /pcf-deploy. Run pack.ps1 from the `Solution/` dir if it is CWD-relative.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>
    W11 task 111 added `enrichUploadStatus` in `services/CommunicationAttachmentsService.ts` + the icon in
